    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "Three meals"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "The day has **el desayuno**, **la comida** and **la cena**. Each has its verb: **desayunar**, **comer**, **cenar**. So I have breakfast is just **desayuno**.\n\nIn Spain la comida is around two and la cena around nine or later.\n\nWhat you eat follows the verb with no article: **desayuno** café con leche y pan. **Como** arroz. **Ceno** huevos.\n\nWith **gustar** the article comes back: me gusta **el** queso; me gustan **las** manzanas.\n\nHunger and thirst take **tener**: **tengo hambre**, **tengo sed**."
      }
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": {"en": "What do you eat?"},
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "¿Qué desayunas?",
          "en": "What do you have for breakfast?",
          "analisis": [["¿Qué", "question"], ["desayunas", "verb"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Café con leche y pan con tomate. ¿Y tú?",
          "en": "White coffee and bread with tomato. And you?",
          "analisis": [["Café con leche", "object"], ["pan con tomate", "object"]]
        },
